## Layout

- `manuscript.qmd` — the manuscript (Quarto manuscript project; render with `quarto render`)
- `data/` - input data
- `figures/` - output figures
- `scripts/` - general scripts
- `binaries/` - program binaries
- `containers/` - apptainer/docker containers
- `references.bib` - bibliography

The recommended folder structure is to name each analysis step by step, e.g. `00_data_mining` or `01_data_mining`. You can be pretty flexible inside of it, but I personally recommend adding specific `notes.qmd` files which serve as a "lab notebook" for that specific analysis, and a `scripts/` folder to hold any reusable code for that specific task
